---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About | UtilX"
  description="About UtilX — free, privacy-first developer tools that run entirely in your browser."
  canonicalPath="/about.html"
>
<main>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About UtilX</h1>
    <p class="lede">UtilX is a small collection of free, single-purpose tools for everyday development tasks: formatting JSON, testing regex, building cron schedules, generating passwords, and converting between common formats.</p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>Most days, developers reach for a search engine to solve a five-second problem — "is this JSON valid," "what does this regex match," "what does this cron expression mean" — and land on a page cluttered with pop-ups, forced sign-ups, or tools that silently upload input to a server. UtilX is the opposite: no accounts, no uploads, no tracking of what you paste in. Every tool runs as plain JavaScript in your own browser tab.</p>

    <h2>How it's funded</h2>
    <p>This site is supported by display advertising. No user data, pasted input, or generated output is ever collected, stored, or sold — see the <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

    <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
    <p>UtilX is an independently run, small-scale project. If you spot a bug or have a tool you'd like added, get in touch via the <a href="/contact.html">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
